  "cycleDesign": "The lathe drive reverses each period: the tool carriage descends along the stock to one work-thread turn below the drawn tool and returns up its groove. Playback opens at the drawn tool position on the first cut (threaded above the tool, plain blank below); that descent cuts one more turn, and every later pass chases the thread down to the same stop, so the rest of the blank stays a plain shank as drawn and the loop never exchanges the work. The route sync rebuilds the cut from the recorded work angle and playback time; one 16 s period closes the loop.",
